WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:16.220
One day Marilla said, "Diana Barry is home, Anne.

2
00:00:16.221 --> 00:00:20.737
I'm going to the Barrys' today. You can come with me and meet Diana."

3
00:00:20.738 --> 00:00:26.522
Anne looked up at Marilla. "I'm nervous! What if Diana doesn't like me?"

4
00:00:26.523 --> 00:00:30.131
"Diana will like you," Marilla said firmly.

5
00:00:30.132 --> 00:00:35.265
"But if Mrs. Barry doesn't like you, it won't matter how much Diana likes you."

6
00:00:35.266 --> 00:00:38.100
Anne and Marilla went to the Barrys' house.

7
00:00:38.101 --> 00:00:43.512
"Come in," Mrs. Barry said cordially. "Is this the girl you've adopted?"

8
00:00:43.513 --> 00:00:46.662
"Yes, this is Anne," said Marilla.

9
00:00:46.663 --> 00:00:49.618
"Spelled with an 'e'," Anne whispered.

10
00:00:49.619 --> 00:00:55.034
When Diana came in, Anne saw she was a pretty girl with a happy face.

11
00:00:55.035 --> 00:01:01.238
"Diana, take Anne to the garden and show her your flowers," said Mrs. Barry.

12
00:01:01.239 --> 00:01:07.523
Outside, Anne and Diana sat among the roses, daffodils, daisies, and violets.

13
00:01:07.524 --> 00:01:13.215
"Oh, Diana," Anne blurted out. "Can I be . . . your best friend?"

14
00:01:13.216 --> 00:01:19.876
Diana laughed. "I guess so," she said. "I'm glad you're living at Green Gables.

15
00:01:19.877 --> 00:01:25.086
There's no other girl who lives close, and my sisters are too little to play with."

16
00:01:25.087 --> 00:01:28.265
"Will you be my friend forever and ever?

17
00:01:28.266 --> 00:01:32.470
We must hold hands—like this," Anne said eagerly.

18
00:01:32.471 --> 00:01:35.972
Diana looked surprised but said, "All right."

19
00:01:35.973 --> 00:01:39.458
"I'll say the oath first," Anne said.

20
00:01:39.459 --> 00:01:48.103
"I promise to always love my dear best friend, Diana Barry, as long as the sun and moon are in the sky."

21
00:01:48.104 --> 00:01:53.232
Diana repeated the oath with a laugh. "You're a strange girl, Anne.

22
00:01:53.233 --> 00:01:56.770
But I think I'm going to like you very much!"

23
00:01:56.771 --> 00:01:59.892
The next day Anne hurried into the house.

24
00:01:59.893 --> 00:02:08.872
"Oh Marilla," she cried, "there's going to be a Sunday school picnic next Wednesday, right near the Lake of Shining Waters.

25
00:02:08.873 --> 00:02:15.864
And Mrs. Lynde is going to make ice cream. Think of it—ice cream! Can I go?"

26
00:02:15.865 --> 00:02:18.847
"Yes, of course," Marilla answered.

27
00:02:18.848 --> 00:02:30.212
"But . . . but . . . ," Anne stammered. "Diana says that everyone must take a basket of things to eat. I can't cook and—"

28
00:02:30.213 --> 00:02:33.710
"I'll bake something for you to bring," said Marilla.

29
00:02:33.711 --> 00:02:39.028
"Oh, you're so kind to me!" Anne exclaimed, kissing Marilla's cheeks.

30
00:02:39.029 --> 00:02:43.495
It was the first time in Marilla's life that a child had kissed her.

31
00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:53.213
She was secretly very pleased at Anne's impulsive show of affection, but she said gruffly, "All right, stop your kissing nonsense."

32
00:02:53.214 --> 00:03:00.231
It was Sunday, three days before the picnic, and Marilla wore her amethyst brooch to church, as usual.

33
00:03:00.232 --> 00:03:03.586
The brooch was Marilla's most treasured possession.

34
00:03:03.587 --> 00:03:08.729
When Anne had first seen the brooch, she'd thought it was very beautiful too.

35
00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:12.809
"Can I hold the brooch for a minute?" she had asked.

36
00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:17.481
"I think amethysts are sweet, like violets!"

37
00:03:17.482 --> 00:03:26.420
On Tuesday evening Marilla was frowning. "Have you seen my amethyst brooch?" she asked Anne. "I can't find it anywhere."

38
00:03:26.421 --> 00:03:32.825
"I saw it this afternoon, when you went out," said Anne a little slowly.

39
00:03:32.826 --> 00:03:38.020
"I was passing by and I saw it, so I went to look at it."

40
00:03:38.021 --> 00:03:41.665
"Did you touch it?" said Marilla sternly.

41
00:03:41.666 --> 00:03:49.563
"Yes," Anne admitted hesitantly. "I pinned it on, just to see how it would look."

42
00:03:49.564 --> 00:03:52.805
"That was wrong, Anne. Where did you put it?"

43
00:03:52.806 --> 00:03:57.597
"I put it near the mirror. I'm sure I put it back," Anne said.

44
00:03:57.598 --> 00:04:04.041
"Well, now it's gone," said Marilla. She looked again, but she didn't see it anywhere.

45
00:04:04.042 --> 00:04:07.221
"Anne, you were the last person to touch it.

46
00:04:07.222 --> 00:04:09.574
Did you take the brooch and lose it?"

47
00:04:09.575 --> 00:04:16.097
"No," said Anne. "I never took your brooch out of the room. That's the truth."

48
00:04:16.098 --> 00:04:21.045
Marilla got angry. "I think you are lying, Anne," she said.

49
00:04:21.046 --> 00:04:25.445
"Go to your room and stay there until you are ready to confess."

50
00:04:25.446 --> 00:04:29.370
"But the picnic is tomorrow, Marilla!" Anne exclaimed.

51
00:04:29.371 --> 00:04:34.149
"I'll stay in my room after the picnic, but I must go to the picnic."

52
00:04:34.150 --> 00:04:39.169
"You aren't going anywhere until you confess," Marilla said firmly.

53
00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:44.038
"Oh, Marilla," gasped Anne. But Marilla had left.

54
00:04:44.039 --> 00:04:48.521
Marilla was worried. She was worried about her valuable brooch.

55
00:04:48.522 --> 00:04:51.280
She was worried that Anne told lies.

56
00:04:51.281 --> 00:04:57.685
Marilla searched the room again, but found nothing. Anne steadfastly refused to confess.

57
00:04:57.686 --> 00:05:01.488
Wednesday was sunny, a perfect day for a picnic.

58
00:05:01.489 --> 00:05:10.212
When Marilla took Anne her breakfast, she found Anne sitting on her bed. "I'm ready to confess," Anne said.

59
00:05:10.213 --> 00:05:16.505
"Ah!" Marilla said. Her punishment had worked, but the success was bitter.

60
00:05:16.506 --> 00:05:22.427
"I took the amethyst brooch," Anne began. "It was so beautiful!

61
00:05:22.428 --> 00:05:27.402
I put it on my dress and pretended I was a beautiful lady who lives in a castle.

62
00:05:27.403 --> 00:05:36.396
I went to the Lake of Shining Waters and the brooch fell off into the water and sank. That's my best confession."

63
00:05:36.397 --> 00:05:43.197
Marilla became very angry. Anne had lost her precious brooch and did not seem sorry at all!

64
00:05:43.198 --> 00:05:47.798
"Anne, you are a very wicked girl," Marilla said.

65
00:05:47.799 --> 00:05:53.668
"Yes, I suppose I am," agreed Anne. "You have to punish me.

66
00:05:53.669 --> 00:05:56.706
Can you punish me quickly so I can go to the picnic?"

67
00:05:56.707 --> 00:06:03.280
Marilla snorted. "Picnic? You're not going to the picnic. That is your punishment."

68
00:06:03.281 --> 00:06:07.045
Anne jumped to her feet. "But you promised me!

69
00:06:07.046 --> 00:06:13.134
Oh, Marilla, I must go to the picnic. That's why I confessed.

70
00:06:13.135 --> 00:06:17.407
Please let me go! There will be ice cream."

71
00:06:17.408 --> 00:06:22.509
"You're not going to the picnic and that's final!" Marilla said.

72
00:06:22.510 --> 00:06:28.109
Anne cried out loudly and flung herself on the bed, crying and crying.

73
00:06:28.110 --> 00:06:32.814
"I believe the child is crazy!" Marilla said as she left the room.

74
00:06:32.815 --> 00:06:36.269
Later Marilla decided to mend a black scarf.

75
00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:39.009
The scarf was in a box near the window.

76
00:06:39.010 --> 00:06:43.470
As Marilla held it up, something sparkled in the sunlight.

77
00:06:43.471 --> 00:06:49.640
Marilla gasped. It was the amethyst brooch, hanging off the end of the scarf.

78
00:06:49.641 --> 00:06:53.433
"I picked up this scarf on Monday," Marilla thought.

79
00:06:53.434 --> 00:06:56.798
"The brooch must have caught onto it."

80
00:06:56.799 --> 00:07:01.075
Marilla rushed to Anne's room. "I've just found my brooch.

81
00:07:01.076 --> 00:07:03.981
What story did you tell me this morning?"

82
00:07:03.982 --> 00:07:09.151
Anne replied, "You said I must stay in my room until I confessed.

83
00:07:09.152 --> 00:07:13.155
So I confessed because I wanted to go to the picnic.

84
00:07:13.156 --> 00:07:18.040
I thought of a good story, but I can't go to the picnic anyway."

85
00:07:18.041 --> 00:07:23.118
Marilla had to laugh. "Anne, you are a surprise!

86
00:07:23.119 --> 00:07:29.499
It was wrong for you to lie, but I understand why, and I should have believed you in the first place.

87
00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:35.696
So if you forgive me, I forgive you. Now get ready for the picnic."

88
00:07:35.697 --> 00:07:38.287
"But isn't it too late?"

89
00:07:38.288 --> 00:07:44.981
"No, it's only two o'clock. Wash your face and comb your hair, and I'll get some food ready."

90
00:07:44.982 --> 00:07:50.209
"Oh, Marilla! Five minutes ago I wished I was never born.

91
00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:53.951
Now I wouldn't change places with an angel!"

92
00:07:53.952 --> 00:07:58.263
That night Anne returned to Green Gables happy and tired.

93
00:07:58.264 --> 00:08:05.672
"It was wonderful. We rowed a boat, and Jane Andrews nearly fell in the lake and drowned.

94
00:08:05.673 --> 00:08:10.809
I wish it was me—how romantic to nearly drown."

95
00:08:10.810 --> 00:08:23.307
After Anne went to bed, Marilla smiled and thought, "It's never boring with Anne around."
